for a  clinical trial  clinical trial personnel we have is  leanora renda she's a dietitian that  works with our patients she's excellent  she did a webinar for the American brain  tumor Association if you're interested I  invite you to go on their website and  listen to it it describes the use of the  ketogenic diet for brain tumors Nerissa  honi dr. Nerissa honey she is a research  clinical nurse and she's doing quality  of life analysis and cognitive analysis  on the patients and quality of life  analysis on the caregivers doctors line  Ashby and Christopher Dardis are the  neuro oncologists at the BNI and of  course the Baron neurosurgeons are  strongly behind this the clinical trial  is for high-grade gliomas we're doing 20  patients with gross total reception 20  patients with a subtotal reception we're  looking at the ketogenic diet plus the  standard of care meaning temozolomide  and radiation using a standard protocol  so that treatment does not change at all  during the radiation chemotherapy the  patients are on a classic 421 ketogenic  diet it's administered by a registered  dietitian that's got training in the  ketogenic diet and that would be lorenda  or in our institution the patients are  doing this with normal food and Keeta  cal as a supplement if they want it the  diet is administered with the use of  something called the keto calculator  this is an online database it's HIPAA  compliant it's free the patients need to  get a prescription from their physician  there then registered on this database  and the dietitian and the patient can  then work together to make meal plans  and look at the different nutrients to  maintain the ketogenic diet in a healthy  way and through the use of the kita  calculator Lee and the patient can work  together in calories and amount of food  is altered as needed for the patient to  feel good and maintained ketone level  and glucose levels where we want them  we're looking at the tolerability of the  diet we're looking at overall and  progression-free survival of the  patient's quality of life of the patient  and the caregiver because this is a bit  of a lifestyle to have to change food  preparation so one of the things that  were  you hear from people who haven't done  this is well it'll be too hard for  people it turns out that the patients  that have been on this many of them say  they can actually do this and it gives  them the feeling that they're doing  something to help themselves and that's  really important for patient quality of  life we're looking at changes in seizure  activity and anti-seizure medications  we're looking at changes in steroid use  the neurocognitive tests as i mentioned  are being done on the patients we're  doing daily blood ketone and blood  glucose levels to monitor the diet  effectiveness and determine if  alterations are needed so the goals that  we have and have the ketone levels above  three preferably around four and glucose  at about 70 now a number of brain tumor  patients end up on steroids because of  swelling first of all we're hoping that  the ketogenic diet will reduce the need  for this but also it can be very  difficult to maintain low glucose levels  in the presence of steroids I'll show  you from some data that I'll give you in  a few minutes that one of our patients  was on that and actually was able to do  it so it might be a little more  difficult but it's not impossible the  patients are monitored for uric acid  cholesterol triglycerides ldh acidosis  and free carnitine so these are the  cases we've had to date to these cases  are actually on our trial and three of  them are being followed outside of our  clinical trial you can see here the the  ages are ranging from 39 to about sixty  three two of them are not on steroids  for them are total follow-up is pretty  variable some of them have just started  one question that we always get that  people really worried about is weight  loss people get very concerned about  weight loss 