of exercise and when she  first got sick she stopped exercising so  there was a little bit of a drop in  weight but once she got strength back  and got back into one more normal  routine that weight was gained back you  can see that even though this patient  was on high-dose steroids her blood  glucose averaged at about 82 it went  ranged from 74 to 105 and the ketones  range from about 5.4 to as low as three  but the outside they averaged about 5.4  they went between point three and 7.7  and even at 7.7 she reported feeling  just fine  cholesterol was borderline high  potassium a little bit low the side  effects that you tend to get with the  ketogenic diet are usually manageable  fairly easily so cholesterol can usually  be managed simply by changing the source  of the fats and constipation is handled  with me relax increases in in calcium or  the are handled with poly citrate and  with that I'm going to just go to my  acknowledgments and open the open the  table for questions I'd like to thank  the people in my laboratory Eric wolf  and Ken Brooks mohammed abdul wahab and  Katie Fenton our students that have done  the majority of the work you saw Katie  curly was college student that did some  of it I mentioned some of the high  school students the de fork with us my  collaborators Philip Stafford Greg  Turner Cheng Wei Lou mark Poole and John  Rowe who first turned me on to the  ketogenic diet and then our funding  sources the first being a really awesome  group of students that work very hard to  raise funds and they actually supported  the work that I was involved with us  getting involved in the ketogenic diet  in the first place and with that I'd be  happy to open the door to questions  there's two questions I see typed the  first is those kita Cal have any effect  on tgf-beta and cytochrome C or a pop  Tata qu'avec in vitro or in vivo we  haven't looked at tgf-beta and we  haven't looked at cytochrome C so I  can't answer that with respect to a pop  ptosis 